A labor of love, given freely: use it, learn from it, self-host it, build on it. Postern is software you run yourself; run it as a network service and the AGPL has you share your changes back, so it stays a commons.

The server core in this repository is AGPL-3.0-only. Three client-side components are permissively MIT-licensed so they are trivial to embed in any codebase: the MCP server @skyphusion/postern-mcp (see mcp/LICENSE), the Python client postern-client (see clients/python/LICENSE), and the IMAP proxy posternimap (imap/, see imap/LICENSE). Each ships its own license file and metadata, which are authoritative for that component.
